an unexpected end to this belarusian  sprinter's olympic run  kristina timanovskaya is seeking asylum  at the polish embassy in tokyo  after she dared to criticize her  national coaching team on instagram  for submitting her into a race without  her consent  and then trying to force her to fly home  to an uncertain fate  she sought police protection at tokyo's  hanada airport as her husband  says he packed his bags and fled belarus  for ukraine  did you ever get the impression that  christina wanted to leave  belarus for good um  yes yes so this wasn't pre-planned  she was cast as hysterical but the  pressure was real  this leaked recording where she begs her  coaches not to make her go  a sinister insight into belarusian  athletics  back in belarus plenty of athletes have  suffered reprisals for supporting the  widespread opposition  to president lukashenko's 27 year rule  so much so there's a support group set  up for them based in  exile in lithuania we have seen examples  of thousands of people who've been  imprisoned for nothing  so i'm sure they would find an article  for christina  she now has a humanitarian visa and will  leave for poland in the coming days  when and if she'll ever get back to  belarus a very different story  diana magnay sky news moscow
 

